:null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"HANDOFF STATE 2026-11-12 06:30 PST: IN PROGRESS. Implemented and verified, but not landed.\n- Gerrit 3366 patch set 3 (0c477221cb694e2a04b45e6c2026a7fc08ce20a5): make verify passed on that exact tree, 04:37-06:14 PST (21142 + 218 passed). Verified is running (Actions run 43235463813).\n- LLM-Review is -1 \"coverage-gap (llm-unavailable)\", not a code finding. The review bot's Bedrock call got AccessDenied from the account's BedrockDailySpendCapDeny policy, which is currently attached to rebar-gerrit-instance-role and the other capped roles. It lifts automatically at 00:00 UTC (16:00 PST).\n- Patch-set history: PS1 got LLM-Review -1 for synthetic ticket titles; fixed with real titles, and the live comparison re-run is recorded on the epic. PS2 got LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1. PS3 drops an absolute local path from the committed results file (it now records the labels file name).\n- Next: after the cap lifts, comment `rerun-llm-review` on 3366 (no new patch set), land at LLM-Review +1 / Verified +1 / 0 unresolved, then tick the AC boxes and close with AWS_PROFILE=frontier-bedrock.\n- Plan review: r4 PASS, certified; claimed.","timestamp":1794493659496061238}],"created_at":1794255945153072001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"2b81edf7-9d9c-4b35-8243-837824e3dee1","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"75af-1212-aa22-463f"},{"link_uuid":"cc1eae42-59bf-48be-89e7-866b13dfb14c","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"05cf-fd45-47fc-437d"},{"link_uuid":"3ecd1b64-e033-450d-a36a-bbcd14177c94","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"7233-7984-3ebf-4daa"},{"link_uuid":"889c95bd-aced-483e-9423-fbe38786b62e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"d5be-953d-a896-43d7"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe point of a second plan-review engine is to compare it with the first. The epic needs a harness that runs both engines on the same plan at the same ref and reports verdict agreement and finding overlap, run once over rebar's own eval corpus. Since [rebar:confident-snooty-stinkpot] both engines return one `plan_review_verdict` contract, and `review_plan(..., engine=..., sign=False, emit_sidecar=False)` runs either one without signing or writing a sidecar.\n\nThe criterion eval specs (`src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/plan-review-*.eval.yaml`) are the wrong corpus. Their cases are single-criterion fragments, mostly without an `## Acceptance Criteria` checklist, so the Layer-1 floor BLOCKs them before either engine runs, and their gold labels say whether ONE criterion fires, not whether the whole plan should block. The whole-plan corpus is the frozen plan-review replay labels file `evals/plan-review-gate/replay/labels-b3784f06….jsonl` (built by `rebar.llm.evals.plan_replay`, ticket celestine-treasonous-ewe). It holds 11 real rebar plans with their reconstructed `description`, `ticket_type`, `file_impact`, empty `children`, and the pipeline's historical `verdict` (7 PASS, 3 BLOCK, 1 INDETERMINATE).\n\n## Approach\n\nNew operator-run harness `src/rebar/llm/evals/engine_comparison.py`: CLI `python -m rebar.llm.evals.engine_comparison` with `--dry-run`, `--limit`, `--labels` (default: the file above), `--out`; never a CI job.\n\n**Corpus.** Rows read straight from the JSONL, ordered by `review_event_ts`, keeping only `verified` rows. The corpus digest is the file's sha256 plus the selected `review_event_uuid`s. `--limit N` keeps the first N in that order but always includes every recorded BLOCK row, so a short run still compares blocking decisions.\n\n**Per item.** Inside `eval_solver.case_store({\"files\": ...})` (the existing disposable git + rebar store, committed, removed on exit), the fixture files are each `file_impact` path's content at the harness checkout's HEAD (`git show HEAD:<path>`; missing paths are skipped and counted). The harness creates one ticket of the row's `ticket_type` with the row's `description` and sets its `file_impact`. It then calls `review_plan(tid, engine=e, sign=False, emit_sidecar=False, repo_root=store, source=\"local\", config=cfg, runner=runner)` for `e` in `(\"pipeline\", \"agentic\")`. Local source: attested mode needs an `origin` remote the store lacks. `cfg` is the operator's `resolve_gate_config()` with `repo_path=store, tickets_path=None`, and `runner` is `get_runner(cfg)` passed through `eval_solver._rerooted(runner, store)` (bug undyed-unheedful-conure). Every file and ticket tool, in both engines, therefore reads the disposable store, never the real rebar repo or its ticket history, while the production model classes still apply (Bedrock with `AWS_PROFILE=frontier-bedrock`).\n\n**Per-engine outcome**, decided in this order. `review_plan` rarely raises: an outage, refusal, auth/config fault or agent budget exhaustion degrades to an unsigned INDETERMINATE.\n1. `error`: a raised exception, or an INDETERMINATE whose coverage has `llm_unavailable`, `input_rejected` or `config_fault`. The bucket is `coverage.resolution_class` when present (agentic failures always carry one since confident-snooty-stinkpot), else `provider_parity.classify_error(coverage.llm_error or str(exc))`. A retryable class (WAIT_AND_RETRY, RETRY_NOW) is retried once after 60 s before it is recorded.\n2. `floor`: `coverage.llm_ran` false with DET blockers.\n3. `indeterminate`: any other INDETERMINATE (`hierarchy_incomplete`, `verify_failed`, `prerequisite_indeterminate`).\n4. Otherwise the verdict (`PASS`/`BLOCK`).\nA run where every outcome on one engine is `error` is marked `\"valid\": false`.\n\n**Checkpointing.** `--out` is rewritten after every item. `--resume` skips rows whose `review_event_uuid` is already recorded with no `error` on either engine.\n\n**Report** (pure functions over the records, unit-tested without a model):\n- Agreement counts only items where both engines produced PASS/BLOCK. Items with an error, a floor outcome or an INDETERMINATE on either side are tallied separately by kind and never scored as disagreement.\n- The 2×2 confusion matrix (pipeline × agentic) and blocking flips (exactly one engine BLOCKs).\n- Finding overlap, summed over items where both engines produced PASS/BLOCK, over each verdict's `blocking` + `advisory` with `tier != \"DET\"`, since the DET floor's findings are identical under both engines. Pairs are matched greedily, highest Jaccard similarity first (ties: pipeline order, then agentic order), on the token sets of each finding's `finding` text (`sidecar._norm_tokens(f[\"finding\"]).split()`) with similarity ≥ `MATCH_THRESHOLD = 0.5`. The threshold is a module constant recorded in the results, not a config key. The report gives matched, pipeline-only and agentic-only counts.\n- Agreement of each engine with the row's recorded historical verdict. It is labelled `historical_pipeline_verdict`, not gold: it came from an older pipeline.\n\n**Output.** JSON with the digest, threshold, per-item records and summary, written to `--out`. The recorded run is `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/engine_comparison_results.json`, with no cost figures. It runs once, live, over all 11 rows (about 4 hours wall time). A summary goes in a comment on the epic. `docs/llm-framework.md` gains a \"Comparing the engines\" section with the command.\n\n## Scope\n\n- src/rebar/llm/evals/engine_comparison.py (new)\n- src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/engine_comparison_results.json (recorded run)\n- tests/unit/test_engine_comparison.py (new)\n- docs/llm-framework.md\n\n## Testing\n\nOffline, with a FakeRunner scripted per engine over a 3-row labels file written in the test:\n\n- Identical PASS verdicts → agreement 1.0, diagonal matrix. Agent `blocker` vs pipeline PASS on one row → agreement 2/3, the off-diagonal cell, 1 flip.\n- Overlap worked example: pipeline findings {A, B, C} and agentic {A′, B′, D} (A′/B′ near-identical) → matched 2, pipeline-only 1, agentic-only 1; a pair below 0.5 does not match; DET findings are excluded.\n- An engine raising on one row, or returning an INDETERMINATE with `llm_unavailable` and `resolution_class` WAIT_AND_RETRY twice → `error` bucketed WAIT_AND_RETRY (retried once), excluded from agreement; an all-error engine marks the run invalid. A floor-blocked row (no AC checklist) → `floor` on both, excluded. An INDETERMINATE → `indeterminate`, excluded.\n- `--limit 1` over rows with one BLOCK keeps that BLOCK row. Historical agreement is computed per engine.\n- `--dry-run` prints the corpus and digest with zero runner calls; `--resume` skips recorded rows.\n- The runner and config each review receives are rooted at the disposable store (`repo_path == store`, `tickets_path is None`). No attestation or sidecar is written in the disposable store.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_engine_comparison.py` passes, pinning outcome precedence, agreement, the confusion matrix, flips, overlap (including DET exclusion and match order), historical agreement, `--limit` and `--dry-run`.\n- [ ] `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/engine_comparison_results.json` is committed from one live run: `python -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/engine_comparison_results.json')); assert len(d['items'])==11 and d['valid'] and not d['dry_run']\"` exits 0.\n- [ ] `docs/llm-framework.md` has a \"Comparing the engines\" section naming the command.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] The live run is summarized in a comment on the epic.\n  provenance: environment=operator workstation (rebar worktree at origin/main); principal=frontier-bedrock AWS profile; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — the harness calls the real Bedrock model classes both engines use in production\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/evals/engine_comparison.py","reason":"new harness"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/engine_comparison_results.json","reason":"recorded run"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_engine_comparison.py","reason":"new tests"},{"path":"docs/llm-framework.md","reason":"how to run"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["depends_on","75af-1212-aa22-463f"],["parent","9794-4336-5ed6-4561"],["relates_to","05cf-fd45-47fc-437d"],["relates_to","7233-7984-3ebf-4daa"],["relates_to","d5be-953d-a896-43d7"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"9794-4336-5ed6-4561","parent_status_uuid":"314b96c1-0ebd-4a14-8404-a39a626237c7","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"b690-7231-22fe-49e4","ticket_type":"story","title":"Engine comparison harness: verdict agreement and finding overlap over the eval corpus","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["496f2503-48f7-4a57-85d4-ef233439657f","26930f4e-1c5d-400a-a4eb-ca3d46b6bf94","f1e78e14-b292-47a7-b312-75ad45ec10e6","e8569bd7-cc1b-4be1-bd51-ffdefc276b42","2043c419-de3c-4fee-8d9e-31376578d311","0845d58c-dc6c-4652-b90e-4b7452d9bffd","314b96c1-0ebd-4a14-8404-a39a626237c7","b232c619-7882-45c1-8403-1ab05a963727","cc1eae42-59bf-48be-89e7-866b13dfb14c","3ecd1b64-e033-450d-a36a-bbcd14177c94","ddbecc6b-d965-49d4-b1dc-c0c2b1008a87","889c95bd-aced-483e-9423-fbe38786b62e"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794493899211500971,"uuid":"f08081f1-ebaf-4e9c-98ed-440c623b93d9"}